# Design system

This project keeps its design system in `{package}/`. Read it before any UI work.

Read order:
1. `{package}/DESIGN.md` — entry file: overview, read order, owner, status, canonical sources.
2. `{package}/tokens.json` — the only source of token values.
3. `{package}/canonical-map.json` — which file or repo path owns each domain and component.
4. `{package}/components/<Component>/README.md` — usage, states, accessibility.

Rules:
- Refer to tokens by name; never copy a token value into code or docs.
- Do not hand-edit the DESIGN.md front matter or viewer.html; regenerate them after token changes:
  `python <plugin>/scripts/build-design-system.py --package {package} --design-md --viewer`
- Check before handing work back: `python <plugin>/scripts/verify-design-system.py --package {package}`
- `<plugin>` is the folder where the agent-design-studio plugin is installed (the one that holds its `scripts/`
  and `skills/`); this project keeps no copy of these scripts. If that folder is unknown, ask the user where the
  plugin is installed. Do not run a file of the same name found in this project instead.

Preview offline: open `{package}/viewer.html` in a browser.
